1
00:00:03,205 --> 00:00:07,777
This is Postmortem Pad, a Fabric App where every pipeline failure of

2
00:00:07,777 --> 00:00:11,475
the last ninety days is a tremor on its system’s trace.

3
00:00:11,925 --> 00:00:15,149
Height is severity, the ring is time to resolve,

4
00:00:15,149 --> 00:00:18,575
and open incidents keep trembling up to the stylus.

5
00:00:19,585 --> 00:00:23,078
Switch the lens to category and one pattern jumps

6
00:00:23,078 --> 00:00:26,785
out: orders ingest keeps breaking on schema changes.

7
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:31,625
The time to resolve lens shows which recoveries dragged on.

8
00:00:32,437 --> 00:00:36,325
Today ranks what needs attention now: the most severe

9
00:00:36,325 --> 00:00:40,287
open incident, the aging ones, and overdue follow-ups.

10
00:00:40,737 --> 00:00:43,087
One click focuses the drum on it and

11
00:00:43,087 --> 00:00:45,567
switches to the lens that explains it.

12
00:00:46,367 --> 00:00:49,676
Viewing as an engineer dims everything that is

13
00:00:49,676 --> 00:00:52,697
not mine and puts my own follow-ups first.

14
00:00:53,537 --> 00:00:56,275
Each incident opens as a black box: started,

15
00:00:56,275 --> 00:00:59,137
detected, now, and the time between each mark.

16
00:00:59,587 --> 00:01:02,373
The transcript highlights wording that points at a

17
00:01:02,373 --> 00:01:05,047
person, with a blameless prompt right beside it.

18
00:01:05,855 --> 00:01:08,749
To resolve it I give three facts: when it

19
00:01:08,749 --> 00:01:11,925
was fixed, why it happened and what fixed it.

20
00:01:12,375 --> 00:01:15,373
The category checklist on its own does not count as

21
00:01:15,373 --> 00:01:17,725
a root cause, so the app stops me there.

22
00:01:18,175 --> 00:01:20,858
With a real root cause the recorder stops,

23
00:01:20,858 --> 00:01:23,285
and the tremor rings down on the drum.

24
00:01:24,092 --> 00:01:30,572
Follow-ups are aftershocks: small spikes after a tremor, red when they are overdue.

25
00:01:31,022 --> 00:01:35,156
The aftershocks page groups them by owner, overdue first,

26
00:01:35,156 --> 00:01:38,202
and ticking one off is instant, with undo.

27
00:01:39,016 --> 00:01:42,706
Fault lines shows the patterns: schema changes lead,

28
00:01:42,706 --> 00:01:45,686
and Monday mornings are when things break.

29
00:01:46,499 --> 00:01:50,392
Log it in two minutes, keep the wording blameless, and

30
00:01:50,392 --> 00:01:53,709
let the seismograph show you what to fix next.
